; fas9_existing_fields.scr - the facit of step 9.2 (plan 2026-10-27-fas-9-typer.md): WIPEOUT, WIPEOUTVARIABLES,
; SCALE, the colours of BLOCK and ENDBLK, and the vertex identifiers (91) of LWPOLYLINE and POLYLINE/VERTEX (F9.21).
;   python -I tools/fas9_facit_run.py doc/facit/fas9_existing_fields.scr
; starts AutoCAD 2025's core on acad.dwt (a new empty drawing). Plain AutoCAD commands, no LISP (see fas9_example.scr).
;
; What the commands of the core cannot do, and what the plan calls "ej testat" because of it:
;  - BLOCK and ENDBLK get a colour only from the anonymous blocks AutoCAD makes (a dimension's *D block takes the
;    dimension's colour on both records); -BLOCK of a coloured circle gives neither. No command makes the two
;    records differ, so a BLOCK with a colour and an ENDBLK without (or two colours) has no AutoCAD file made here
;    (build/test-data/local-r13r14/7H12R10F_schneider_r14_dimension_spline.dxf, an AutoCAD R14 file, is the one
;    observation: BLOCK 62 = 7, ENDBLK none). F9.21 asks for the 1024 case: AutoCAD wrote no such flag anywhere
;    (70 = 1 on every constrained polyline), so there is no file for it.
;  - PEDIT's vertex editing ("Edit vertex") needs visible vertices: a vertex is added with CHAMFER and removed
;    with BREAK instead. OVERKILL is not in the core.
;  - Snaps and picks need a window the core does not have: AUTOCONSTRAIN on the last object gives the vertices
;    their identifiers (GCFIX at an endpoint does not work here).
;
; --- WIPEOUT and WIPEOUTVARIABLES: a polygon, the frame variable 0 / 1 / 2, rotated, scaled, mirrored, from a polyline
_.WIPEOUT
0,0
50,0
50,30
10,40
_Close
_.ZOOM
_E
;EXPECT WIPEOUT WIPEOUTVARIABLES
;SAVE wipeout
_.WIPEOUTFRAME
0
;SAVE wipeout frame0
_.WIPEOUTFRAME
2
;SAVE wipeout frame2
_.WIPEOUTFRAME
1
_.ROTATE
_L

0,0
30
_.ZOOM
_E
;SAVE wipeout rotated
_.SCALE
_L

0,0
2
_.ZOOM
_E
;SAVE wipeout scaled
_.MIRROR
_L

0,0
0,10
_Yes
_.ZOOM
_E
;SAVE wipeout mirrored
_.RECTANG
100,100
140,130
_.WIPEOUT
_Polyline
_L
_Yes
_.ZOOM
_E
;SAVE wipeout from_polyline
;
; --- SCALE: three scales with other numbers than 1:n, then one removed (the list is renumbered by AutoCAD)
_.-SCALELISTEDIT
_Add
1:7
1:7
_Add
3 to 2
3:2
_Add
5/16 in = 1 ft
0.3125:12
_Exit
;SAVE scales
_.-SCALELISTEDIT
_Delete
1:7
_Exit
;SAVE scales deleted
;
